※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=64 diag=none

※ A run of eight bytes, whose last element is the one that goes past.  Eight
※ bytes is half a register on every machine here, so the answer about that
※ element sits in the half a target reading the cheaper way would not look at --
※ which is exactly what one of them did, and is why this is its own test rather
※ than a line in another.

let v: u8⟦8⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8, 3u8, 4u8, 5u8, 6u8, 7u8, 60u8⟧

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let up: u8⟦8⟧ = v + 200u8
    up⟦0⟧
